3. Modules and Reusable Task Functions

"type": "module": Adding this to package.json enables ECMAScript Modules (ESM), allowing the use of import and export instead of Node's legacy require().
Exports and Imports: Use export function... to expose logic and import { func } from './file.js' to use it elsewhere. ESM requires the .js extension in relative import paths.
Separation of concerns: Separating data arrays, processing logic, and server startup makes code testable and easier to maintain.
Returning values: Functions should return processed data rather than calling console.log, allowing the caller (like an API route) to decide how to format or send the result.

// src/taskManager.js
export function getAllTasks(tasks) {
  return tasks;
}

export function getTaskById(tasks, id) {
  return tasks.find(task => task.id === id);
}

export function getCompletedTasks(tasks) {
  return tasks.filter(task => task.completed === true);
}

